tion of a Novel Artificial Intelligence System to Monitor and Assess Energy and Macronutrient Intake in Hospitalised Older Patients#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)#{1}":[36,37],"#Evaluation of a Novel Artificial Intelligence System to Monitor and Assess Energy and Macronutrient Intake in Hospitalised Older Patients#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[38,40],"#Evaluation of a Novel Artificial Intelligence System to Monitor and Assess Energy and Macronutrient Intake in Hospitalised Older Patients#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[39,40],"#Evaluation of a Novel Artificial Intelligence System to Monitor and Assess Energy and Macronutrient Intake in Hospitalised Older Patients#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/3GHE3YX7","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/HSF6TBSA?page=1&annotation=4TN4TZZY","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/HSF6TBSA?page=1&annotation=GLBM2GK3","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/HSF6TBSA?page=1&annotation=KEBB7WIN","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 14","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/HSF6TBSA?page=14&annotation=3HPQBQWS","line":39}],"metadata":{"Title":"Evaluation of a Novel Artificial Intelligence System to Monitor and Assess Energy and Macronutrient Intake in Hospitalised Older Patients","Authors":"Ioannis Papathanail, Jana Brühlmann, Maria F. Vasiloglou, Thomai Stathopoulou, Aristomenis K. Exadaktylos, Zeno Stanga, Thomas Münzer, Stavroula Mougiakakou","Year":2021,"DOI":"10.3390/nu13124539","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":". In this study, we propose an automated Artificial Intelligence (AI)-based system that receives input images of the meals before and after their consumption and is able to estimate the patient’s energy, carbohydrate, protein, fat, and fatty acids intake. The system jointly segments the images into the different food components and plate types, estimates the volume of each component before and after consumption, and calculates the energy and macronutrient intake for every meal, based on the kitchen’s menu databas","Findings":"he results from both our system and the hospital’s standard procedure were compared to the estimations of experts.","Conclusions":"Agreement was better with the system, suggesting that it has the potential to replace standard clinical procedures with a positive impact on time spent directly with the patients.The system offers high accuracy, provides the results in an automatic manner, and holds the potential to lower the cost of dietary assessment in a hospitalised environment; therefore, the system could contribute towards enhanced dietary monitoring and assessment of hospitalised patients at risk of malnutrition.","Limitations":"","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"nlsbq3","at":1774939748924},"key":"Augmented Dietitian/papathanailEvaluationNovelArtificial2021a.md"},
